// The same reason in a position that did NOT motivate it. A criterion checked
// only against the fixture that produced it proves nothing about the criterion;
// this row is the foreign one, and it passes because the rule is stated over the
// PROPERTY - a type annotation with a trailing `chip` - rather than over the shape
// that was reported.
fn f(b: [u8; 4] chip writes) { println(b[0] as int); }
fn main() { f([0 as u8; 4]); }
